# A deployment checkout IS a git repo, and operators keep their environment
# backups and the bootstrapped admin credentials right next to it. Plain
# ".env" matches only that one name, so a dated backup or a ".bak" copy shows
# up as an untracked file that a single `git add -A` would commit - carrying
# the Google client secret, the database password and the platform-admin
# password into the repository. Match the whole family, not just the
# canonical name.
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
.admin-credentials
